<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Aukland lifts year earnings.</title>
<headline>Aukland lifts year earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30 vs 11</p>
<p>months to June 30 1995</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     5.8	   vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)  2.0 making 2.0	   vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   4.22	  vs 2.17</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   6.76	  vs 3.51</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.50	  vs 1.33</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.75	  vs 0.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		  66.21	 vs 38.04</p>
<p>Div payable November 1</p>
<p>on register October 18</p>
<p>Full name: Aukland Investments Ltd (development capital)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it was confident of growth in 1997 and said orders were satisfactory.</p>
<p>It reiterated a cautionary issued earlier this month that it was in talks which could have an impact on its share price and urged shareholders to exercise caution in their dealings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
